# Active engine plan

## TODO — independent /verbose controls for tools and providers

- [ ] Make `/verbose` expose three independent options: `tools on|off`, `nvidia on|off`, and `gemini on|off`.
- [ ] Tool-output visibility:
  - `tools on`: display the tool command and its returned output, including errors.
  - `tools off`: display the tool command but suppress its returned output. Example: show `git status`, hide `fatal: not a git repository ...`.
  - This is display-only. Execute tools normally and pass their complete results to the model; do not discard or alter tool results because visibility is off.
- [ ] Enforce **no persistent tool-output**: keep retained tool output in RAM for the active session only. Never create `.artifacts` directories or temporary output-spool files. Discard retained output when the session closes. Keep the existing limits: 16 MiB per output and 64 MiB per session; do not retain oversized output. Leave pre-existing `.artifacts` directories untouched. Normal compressed session history remains disk-backed.
- [ ] NVIDIA and Gemini toggles control only their own thought-summary visibility; keep them independent from each other and from the tools toggle.
- [ ] Do not change `StreamingMode`, streaming speed, or terminal/TUI rendering behavior.
- [ ] Update command descriptions, subcommand completion, persistence/config wiring, and focused tests for all three independent toggles and both tool-output display states.
- [ ] Verify `/verbose` itself does not execute tools or change unrelated settings.
